# Microsoft Enterprise Telegram Voice AI Bot - Project Architecture

## Project Overview

This is a **Microsoft Enterprise Telegram Voice AI Bot** - a multi-million dollar enterprise project that:

- Accepts text, voice, and video note messages
- Processes them through OpenAI (Whisper STT, GPT-4 LLM, TTS)
- Responds with **circular video notes** (512x512) featuring audio visualization
- Uses FFmpeg for video generation with 3 visualization styles: waveform, simple, branded
- **Enterprise-grade architecture** with Microsoft Azure integration
- **High-scale production deployment** with enterprise monitoring and compliance

## Core Architecture Principles

### Service-Oriented Architecture

- **No classes for business logic** - use module.exports with dependency injection
- All services are singletons exported from their files
- Services are located in `src/services/`
- Each service has a single responsibility

### File Structure

```
src/
├── config/           # Configuration and OpenAI client setup
├── controllers/      # Webhook handlers (text, voice, video messages)
├── services/         # Business logic (STT, LLM, TTS, Media, Video)
├── utils/            # Utilities (logger, error handler, file utils)
├── types/            # TypeScript type definitions
├── scripts/          # Helper scripts (webhook management)
└── index.ts          # Application entry point
```

## Key Services

### 1. STT Service ([stt.service.ts](mdc:src/services/stt.service.ts))

- Transcribes audio files using OpenAI Whisper
- Validates audio files (max 25MB)
- Supports OGG, MP3, WAV formats

### 2. LLM Service ([llm.service.ts](mdc:src/services/llm.service.ts))

- Generates AI responses using GPT-4
- Maintains in-memory conversation history
- Implements conversation window (last N messages)

### 3. TTS Service ([tts.service.ts](mdc:src/services/tts.service.ts))

- Converts text to speech using OpenAI TTS
- Supports 6 voice options (alloy, echo, fable, onyx, nova, shimmer)
- Max 4096 characters per request

### 4. Media Service ([media.service.ts](mdc:src/services/media.service.ts))

- Downloads files from Telegram servers
- Converts audio formats using FFmpeg
- Manages file cleanup

### 5. Video Service ([video.service.ts](mdc:src/services/video.service.ts))

- Creates circular video notes (512x512)
- Three visualization styles: waveform, simple, branded
- Uses FFmpeg for video generation

## Message Processing Pipeline

### Text Message Flow:

```
Text Input → LLM → TTS → Video Generation → Send Video Note
```

### Voice Message Flow:

```
Voice Input → Download → STT → LLM → TTS → Video Generation → Send Video Note
```

### Video Note Flow:

```
Video Note → Download → Extract Audio → STT → LLM → TTS → Video Generation → Send Video Note
```

## Configuration

### Environment Variables ([env.ts](mdc:src/config/env.ts))

All configuration is loaded from `.env` file with validation:

- `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` - Telegram bot token
- `OPENAI_API_KEY` - OpenAI API key (must start with `sk-`)
- `WEBHOOK_URL` - Must end with `/webhook`
- `VIDEO_STYLE` - waveform | simple | branded
- `TTS_VOICE` - alloy | echo | fable | onyx | nova | shimmer
- `CONVERSATION_WINDOW` - Number of messages in memory (default: 10)

### OpenAI Client ([openai.ts](mdc:src/config/openai.ts))

Configured OpenAI client with:

- Automatic retries (3 attempts)
- 60 second timeout
- Exported constants for Whisper, GPT, and TTS

## Error Handling

### Custom Error Types ([errorHandler.ts](mdc:src/utils/errorHandler.ts))

- `STTError` - Speech-to-text failures
- `LLMError` - Language model failures
- `TTSError` - Text-to-speech failures
- `MediaError` - Media processing failures
- `VideoError` - Video generation failures

### Error Handling Strategy

- Service-level try-catch blocks
- User-friendly error messages sent to Telegram
- Structured error logging with context
- Automatic file cleanup on errors

## Logging

### Logger ([logger.ts](mdc:src/utils/logger.ts))

- Structured logging with levels: error, warn, info, debug
- Development: Colored console output
- Production: JSON format
- Never log sensitive data (API keys, tokens)

### Log Context

Always include:

- `chatId` - Telegram chat ID
- `userId` - Telegram user ID
- `duration` - Operation duration in milliseconds
- Error details when applicable

## File Management

### Temporary Files

- Location: `tmp/` directory
- Auto-cleanup on startup (files older than 24 hours)
- Cleanup after each message processing
- Use `getTempFilePath(extension)` for unique names

### File Naming Convention

```
download-{timestamp}-{random}.ogg
tts-{timestamp}-{random}.mp3
{timestamp}-{random}-video.mp4
```

## TypeScript Guidelines

### Type Safety

- All functions must have explicit return types
- Use interfaces from [types/index.ts](mdc:src/types/index.ts)
- No `any` types except for FFmpeg callbacks
- Enable strict mode in tsconfig.json

### Async/Await

- Always use async/await (not callbacks)
- Handle errors with try-catch
- Return promises directly (avoid `return await`)

## Webhook Management

### Entry Point ([index.ts](mdc:src/index.ts))

- Express server on port 3000 (configurable)
- POST `/webhook` - Telegram webhook endpoint
- GET `/health` - Health check
- GET `/status` - Detailed status with stats
- Graceful shutdown handling

### Controller ([webhook.controller.ts](mdc:src/controllers/webhook.controller.ts))

Handlers for:

- `message:text` - Text messages
- `message:voice` - Voice messages
- `message:video_note` - Video notes
- Commands: `/start`, `/clear`, `/help`

## Development Workflow

### Local Development

1. Start server: `npm run dev`
2. Start ngrok: `ngrok http 3000`
3. Update `WEBHOOK_URL` in `.env`
4. Set webhook: `npm run webhook:set`

### Scripts

- `npm run dev` - Development server with hot reload
- `npm run build` - Compile TypeScript
- `npm start` - Production server
- `npm run webhook:set` - Set Telegram webhook
- `npm run webhook:info` - Check webhook status

## Important Notes

### Memory Management

- Conversation history stored in-memory (Map)
- Bounded by CONVERSATION_WINDOW setting
- Consider Redis for horizontal scaling

### Performance Considerations

- Total response time: 10-20 seconds
- STT: 2-5 seconds
- LLM: 1-3 seconds
- TTS: 1-3 seconds
- Video generation: 2-5 seconds (waveform), 1-2 seconds (simple)

### Dependencies

- express - HTTP server
- grammy - Telegram bot framework
- openai - OpenAI API client
- fluent-ffmpeg - FFmpeg wrapper
- ffmpeg-static - FFmpeg binary

## When Adding New Features

1. **Create a service** in `src/services/` if it's business logic
2. **Add types** to `src/types/index.ts`
3. **Update controller** in `src/controllers/webhook.controller.ts`
4. **Add error handling** with custom error types
5. **Add logging** with appropriate context
6. **Update documentation** in relevant .md files
7. **Test manually** with Telegram bot

## Common Patterns

### Service Pattern

```typescript
export class ServiceName {
  async methodName(param: Type): Promise<ReturnType> {
    const startTime = Date.now();
    try {
      logger.info('Operation started', { param });
      // Implementation
      const duration = Date.now() - startTime;
      logger.info('Operation completed', { duration });
      return result;
    } catch (error) {
      logger.error('Operation failed', { error });
      throw new CustomError('Error message');
    }
  }
}

export const serviceName = new ServiceName();
```

### File Cleanup Pattern

```typescript
const filesToCleanup: string[] = [];
try {
  const file = await generateFile();
  filesToCleanup.push(file);
  // Process file
} finally {
  await mediaService.deleteFiles(filesToCleanup);
}
```

